NAME
     join - join two files on a common field

SYNOPSIS
     join [-a N] [-v N] [-t C] [-1 N] [-2 N] FILE1 FILE2

DESCRIPTION
     join reads two sorted files and, for each pair of lines whose join
     field matches, writes the field followed by the rest of both lines.

OPTIONS
     -1 N   the join field in FILE1
     -2 N   the join field in FILE2
     -t C   fields are separated by C
     -a N   also print the unpaired lines of file N
     -v N   print only the unpaired lines of file N

SEE ALSO
     sort(1), comm(1), awk(1)
